(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[14 1 "// The module _signal (PY6f; Modules/signalmodule.c): the process's signals delivered to Python handlers."] [15 1 "// signal(n, callable) has os/signal notify one channel; its receiver goroutine marks the signal pending (the C"] [16 1 "// handler's trip_signal), sets the eval breaker, wakes the main thread when it blocks and writes the wakeup fd;"] [17 1 "// the main thread runs the handlers at its next check (thread_gil.go). SIG_IGN is signal.Ignore, SIG_DFL"] [18 1 "// signal.Reset. raise_signal and os.kill of the own process run the handler before they return, as on Linux."] [19 1 "// The interval timers (alarm, setitimer) are Go timers sending the signal; pthread_sigmask's mask is kept here:"] [20 1 "// a blocked signal stays pending (sigpending, sigwait) until unblocked."] [26 1 "// sysPidfdSendSignal is pidfd_send_signal's syscall number (424 on linux/amd64 and linux/arm64)"] [31 39 "// the main thread's wake-up from a blocking wait"] [32 39 "// any arrival (sigwait)"] [33 39 "// tripped, its handler to run"] [34 39 "// is_tripped"] [35 39 "// pthread_sigmask's mask"] [36 39 "// arrived while blocked (sigpending)"] [37 39 "// notified on sigCh"] [38 39 "// arrivals so far (pidfd_send_signal's wait)"] [39 39 "// set_wakeup_fd's fd, -1 none"] [40 39 "// set_wakeup_fd's warn_on_full_buffer"] [41 39 "// the errno of a failed write to the wakeup fd, its report pending (0 none)"] [43 2 "// sigHandlers are the Python-level handlers (Handlers[n].func), touched under the GIL"] [45 21 "// default_int_handler"] [51 2 "// SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ ignored at the start, before any import of signal, as CPython's _PySignal_Init does with"] [52 2 "// install_signal_handlers (py-design-1122: a write to a closed pipe is a BrokenPipeError, json.tool's exit status"] [53 2 "// EPIPE, not the signal's death); _signal's import records them as SIG_IGN"] [57 1 "// blockedMask is pthread_sigmask's mask as a kernel sigset (py-mp-1125): a child started by ForkExec (fork_exec,"] [58 1 "// posix_spawn without setsigmask, spawnv) gets it, as a C process's child inherits its thread's mask."] [69 1 "// startSignals starts the receiver once."] [82 1 "// ownSignalHook, when set, handles a signal pyi sends itself (killSignal of its own pid, raise_signal) before the"] [83 1 "// signal module does (queue 220: faulthandler's handlers, and the default action that ends the process): handled true"] [84 1 "// and the call returns."] [87 1 "// signalTakenHook, when set, says a signal's handler is another module's (queue 220: faulthandler.register without"] [88 1 "// chain replaces the Python handler, as its sigaction does): the Python handler is not tripped."] [91 1 "// deliverSignal is the C handler: held when blocked, else tripped; the wakeup fd written."] [113 1 "// wakeupWrite is trip_signal's write of the signal's number to the wakeup fd (_Py_write_noraise: EINTR retried): a"] [114 1 "// failure is reported, as the pending call report_wakeup_write_error does, at the main thread's next check"] [115 1 "// (runPendingSignals: an unraisable OSError, queue 595), unless the buffer is full and warn_on_full_buffer is off."] [133 1 "// wakeupReport is report_wakeup_write_error, the pending call a failed write to the wakeup fd left (queue 595)."] [140 1 "// ExtRaiseSignal is raise(sig) of C code in pyi's C world (arbace/pyctypes; queue 594: _testcapi's"] [141 1 "// raise_SIGINT_then_send_None) for a signal the C world left at its default action: the process's signals are"] [142 1 "// Python's, so a signal with a Python handler is delivered as the kernel runs CPython's C handler inside raise (the"] [143 1 "// handler tripped, or held while blocked) and its Python handler runs at the next check, not before raise returns;"] [144 1 "// false for any other signal (the C world's default action ends the process)."] [147 3 "// a signal the process ignores (SIG_IGN, also one ignored since its start: a SIGINT a non-interactive shell's"] [148 3 "// asynchronous command inherits) is discarded, as the kernel discards it; not the C world's default action"] [149 3 "// (py-small-1127: test_generators' test_raise_and_yield_from killed the driver, status 130)"] [157 33 "// musl's raise is tkill"] [162 1 "// tripSignal marks n pending and wakes the main thread (trip_signal)."] [174 1 "// runPendingSignals is _PyErr_CheckSignalsTstate on the main thread: each tripped signal's Python handler"] [175 1 "// called with the signal and the running frame; an exception from one leaves the rest tripped for later."] [184 2 "// _Py_HandlePending: the signals' handlers, then the pending calls (a failed wakeup write's report); a handler's"] [185 2 "// exception leaves the report for the next check (sigAny kept)"] [197 4 "// no Python handler by the time the check runs (bpo-43406): interrupt_main's tripped signal after"] [198 4 "// _PySignal_Fini, or a handler replaced since; an unraisable error, never the signal's action"] [219 1 "// signalFini is _PySignal_Fini (Py_FinalizeEx's, before finalize_modules: queue 595, test_signal's"] [220 1 "// test__thread_interrupt_main): every handler cleared and its tripped mark dropped, a Python handler's signal back to"] [221 1 "// its default action; a __del__ at the modules' clearing that calls interrupt_main then finds no handler (the race"] [222 1 "// condition's unraisable OSError, runPendingSignals)."] [238 1 "// setOSHandler makes the process's action for n follow its Python handler and the mask: notified when a"] [239 1 "// callable handles it or it is blocked, else ignored or the default."] [263 3 "// SIG_DFL is the default action, also for a signal ignored at the start that Go's Reset leaves ignored"] [264 3 "// (py-mods-1122)"] [271 1 "// exitSigint is Modules/main.c's exit_sigint after an unhandled KeyboardInterrupt (queue 231): SIGINT's default action"] [272 1 "// restored and the signal sent to the process, so that its parent sees it killed by SIGINT; else exit status 130."] [278 38 "// delivered to this thread on the call's return; another one's at the latest here"] [283 1 "// killSignal is kill(pid, sig). The own process's signal with a Python handler, not blocked, is delivered here"] [284 1 "// and its handler run before kill returns, as the kernel delivers it to the calling thread before kill returns"] [285 1 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches the handler)."] [300 3 "// blocked: pending when kill returns, as the kernel makes it (queue 231: sigpending right after saw nothing, the"] [301 3 "// signal still on its way through Go's handler thread)"] [311 1 "// the interval timers (ITIMER_REAL, ITIMER_VIRTUAL, ITIMER_PROF), counted in wall time"] [325 1 "// setItimer arms which's timer (value 0 disarms), returning the old value and interval."] [344 3 "// disarmed: an expiry not yet handled is dropped, as the kernel's single pending bit is taken by the"] [345 3 "// handler that disarms it"] [366 5 "// a Python handler: delivered here, under the timer's lock, so a disarmed timer sends no more"] [367 5 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches it)"] [396 2 "// the start installs SIGINT's handler (py-os-1124; pylifecycle's init_signals, _PySignal_Init: a program that never"] [397 2 "// imports signal ends with KeyboardInterrupt at a SIGINT, not by the signal; test_subprocess's test_send_signal)"] [418 4 "// as at CPython's start: SIGINT's default_int_handler, SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ ignored, the rest SIG_DFL"] [424 4 "// a SIGHUP ignored at the process's start (nohup, a parent's SIG_IGN): SIG_IGN, as CPython's signal_get_set_handlers"] [425 4 "// reads it (py-mods-1122)"] [430 4 "// SIGINT's default_int_handler, unless the process started with SIGINT ignored (signal_install_handlers sets it"] [431 4 "// only over SIG_DFL: a child of nohup or of a SIG_IGN keeps ignoring it)"] [551 5 "// the C handler runs inside raise(): the Python handler before raise_signal returns"] [574 4 "// set_wakeup_fd(fd, /, *, warn_on_full_buffer=True)"] [694 5 "// only the main thread runs handlers: wait for any arrival"] [698 4 "// until a signal is pending (a stale wake-up token is not one)"] [751 7 "// delivered on unblocking: the default action or nothing"] [810 5 "// the own process's signal (a pidfd of another process times out here, harmlessly) handled"] [811 5 "// before the call returns, as the kernel delivers it"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[54 82] [61 12] [61 22] [74 35] [108 26] [122 35] [135 28] [150 38] [191 12] [191 22] [210 60] [224 12] [224 22] [259 22] [288 40] [305 50] [420 14] [420 24] [468 31] [483 14] [483 24] [485 39] [510 40] [532 26] [546 40] [557 63] [603 37] [621 32] [636 31] [678 37] [727 14] [727 24] [756 40] [798 35] [806 104] [813 16] [813 61]]} (go/file "builtins_signal.go" :imports [


